comments.body:
@tolot27 That's not the request.
The request is to represent the blood glucose graphically with more than the current 3 colors.  Right now, we see all the in range measurements in blue, all the lows in red, and all the highs in orange.

This is a request.  We may disagree with the priority for implementing it.  But, it is a valid request.  There are so many request that re open.  Why shouldn't this?

@Navid200 I think I understand the request, even if it is not precise enough:

@bryanw20 requested:
> add more levels, then we can have more colors on the graph.

He did not mention whether he just want additional threshold lines and/or coloring the BG values according to a certain threshold. In any way, he wants to have additional bins of the BG value range (mathematically speaking) visually separated. That's what I read from his request.

I'm not against reopening this issue. My concern is about the added value from the medical point of view. Also, it should not irritate the users. Most of us expect two thresholds. Making it configurable adds more settings to the already long list of preferences. 
IMHO, only a very small user group, if not just a single user, will have a benefit of such a feature.
